Although 10.0 lb weight is a little much, I don't mind wearing vampire drag <p></p><i></i></td></tr><tr bgcolor=#cccb9b><td nowrap width=20% valign=top align=left><span class=title> <A HREF=http://pub50.ezboard.com/uschnappfoo.showPublicProfile?language=EN>schnappfoo</A></span><br> <span class=usertitle>Registered User</span><br> <font color=#330000>(5/15/01 5:46:23 pm)</font><br>   <a href=http://pub50.ezboard.com/fgoldenlegionfrm2.showAddReplyScreenFromWeb?topicID=54.topic&index=7>Reply</a>   </td><td valign=top align=left class=m><span class=title> Re: TOFS 7</span><hr size=1> oh yah, forgot about the staff as a drop, oh well<br>
<br>
about the 7th lvl key that she drops...when you zone to the first floor, behind the spectres, there is the mirror that goes up to the 2nd floor.  if you go to the left mirror instead of the right mirror behind the specs and use the tserrina key it takes you to 7th.<br>
<br>
yah, i forgot to mention something.  even though she conned white to me at 51, she still resisted roughly 5 malises, 5 malisements, and 7 malosis from my mage (i just cycled through my debuffs). so im thinking take zilben.  <br>
<br>
the orb isnt a focus item from what i can tell, and ive tried a lot of different things with it, ive wasted a good amount of malachites resummoning pets with it.  the nice thing about it though is if you cast a lvl 49 mage pet (i hear it works with 39 to 49 spells) and then use the reclaim energy, it gives you back a small bit of mana more than it took to cast.  it doesnt work on the 51+ pets and its a waste of a lot of malachites for a bit of mana, hehe<br>
<br>
just some more of my (generaly worthless) wisdom<br>
<br>
Inotuu <p></p><i></i></td></tr><tr bgcolor=#deddbf><td nowrap width=20% valign=top align=left><span class=title> Tressia</span><br> <span class=usertitle>Unregistered User</span><br> <font color=#330000>(5/16/01 6:03:43 am)</font><br>   <a href=http://pub50.ezboard.com/fgoldenlegionfrm2.showAddReplyScreenFromWeb?topicID=54.topic&index=8>Reply</a>   </td><td valign=top align=left class=m><span class=title> 7th floor</span><hr size=1> :waves at everyone::<br>
So when we wanna do this?  Zilben, think we have the lvl manpower to hit her soon - 2 groups?<br>
<br>
*Tressia <p></p><i></i></td></tr><tr bgcolor=#cccb9b><td nowrap width=20% valign=top align=left><span class=title> <A HREF=http://pub50.ezboard.com/uzilben.showPublicProfile?language=EN>Zilben</A></span><br> <span class=usertitle>Registered User</span><br> <font color=#330000>(5/16/01 9:33:59 am)</font><br>   <a href=http://pub50.ezboard.com/fgoldenlegionfrm2.showAddReplyScreenFromWeb?topicID=54.topic&index=9>Reply</a>   </td><td valign=top align=left class=m><span class=title> Re: 7th floor</span><hr size=1> The only thing I worry about is that all the successful kills of her I read about had a warrior or two..both about lvl 49-55, and a cleric or 2 CH'ing the warriors. I recall only 2 warriors. Meakkon and Deadric. Both not near us in lvls atm for a mob like this. Almost all big attacks I know of have warriors soaking up the damage from the uber-mob while clerics heal, and nukers nuking, etc. I know rangers are 'tanks'...but not nearly as good as warriors since rangers pretty much have similar HP to druids. It's not that I don't think we can take her, I just think we have to be very very careful about a mob who can hit for up 220dmg a swing. And she most likely swings approx 2 or 3 times per attack. We'd need probably 2 groups, chanter mandatory, to break pet charms etc, clerics mandatory, as many as possible, as many tanks as we can muster. And the rest whoever wants to go with min lvl 45...I'd like to say min lvl 48, but we don't got enough peeps that high.<br>
So, I leave it up to consensus, is GL rdy for a bigger practice mob...(gate, summon, PC/NPC charm, 220dmg/hit, fear, adds from the rest of the floor, etc...)<br>
<br>
*Gnome <p></p><i></i></td></tr><tr bgcolor=#deddbf><td nowrap width=20% valign=top align=left><span class=title> <A HREF=http://pub50.ezboard.com/uzilben.showPublicProfile?language=EN>Zilben</A></span><br> <span class=usertitle>Registered User</span><br> <font color=#330000>(5/16/01 9:35:55 am)</font><br>   <a href=http://pub50.ezboard.com/fgoldenlegionfrm2.showAddReplyScreenFromWeb?topicID=54.topic&index=10>Reply</a>   </td><td valign=top align=left class=m><span class=title> Re: 7th floor</span><hr size=1> Reason I'm concerned is a corpse recovery from floor 7 is not fun if the person with the keys didn't camp out FAST or gate out.<br>
I'd rather be over-equipped than iffy about the whole thing. <p></p><i></i></td></tr><tr bgcolor=#cccb9b><td nowrap width=20% valign=top align=left><span class=title> tressia</span><br> <span class=usertitle>Unregistered User</span><br> <font color=#330000>(5/16/01 11:48:40 am)</font><br>   <a href=http://pub50.ezboard.com/fgoldenlegionfrm2.showAddReplyScreenFromWeb?topicID=54.topic&index=11>Reply</a>   </td><td valign=top align=left class=m><span class=title> sad</span><hr size=1> Yes, I agree with you zilben - so Tserinna on backburner  <p></p><i></i></td></tr><tr bgcolor=#deddbf><td nowrap width=20% valign=top align=left><span class=title> Tressia</span><br> <span class=usertitle>Unregistered User</span><br> <font color=#330000>(5/30/01 12:58:38 pm)</font><br>   <a href=http://pub50.ezboard.com/fgoldenlegionfrm2.showAddReplyScreenFromWeb?topicID=54.topic&index=12>Reply</a>   </td><td valign=top align=left class=m><span class=title> we're going in</span><hr size=1> See raid folder for times and dates<br>
